.TH GRMODELS 1
.SH NAME
grmodels \- CSprite mesh generator (ball and man)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/grmodels
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Grmodels
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Apps/GrModels
suite (Models, BallGen, ManGen), a generator of
.B SPT_MESH
CSprite models.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The opening page offers two buttons,
.B Man
and
.BR Ball .
Choose one with the mouse, the arrow keys and Enter, or the
.B m
and
.B b
shortcuts.
.PP
Each generator first presents its parameter form.
BallGen asks for radius (default 20), longitude faces (16) and
lattitude rings (8); as in the original, the two counts are halved
before tessellation.
ManGen has 28 fields: 12 body dimensions and 16 joint angles
(shoulders, hips, elbows, knees, wrists and ankles, each side),
defaulting to the original's walking pose.
Move between fields with the arrow keys, Tab or Enter; type digits,
.B .
and
.B \-
to edit; backspace deletes and ctl-u clears.
Esc accepts the form; Del or
.B q
aborts back to the menu.
.PP
Next comes the
.I PopUpColorLighting
chooser (once for the ball's face color; four times for the man's
Shirt, Pants, Skin and Shoes), offering each of the sixteen colors in
single- or double-sided and full- or half-range lighting variants,
exactly as in TempleOS.
Click a swatch or use the arrows and Enter; Esc cancels the whole
generation.
.PP
The mesh is built with the original geometry: the stagger-quad UV
sphere with shared-vertex dedup, or the articulated box man whose
limbs chain shoulder to elbow to wrist and hip to knee to ankle
through Z, Y then X rotations.
It is then displayed shaded by a transliteration of the TempleOS
.I DCLighting
rule: the face normal is dotted with the default light source
(1,1,1)/sqrt(3) and the result dithered between black, the chosen
color and its intensity complement, honouring the two-sided and
half-range flags.
The ball's vertex count is printed, and
.B Do another (Y/N)?
loops back to the form
.RB ( y ,
retaining edits) or returns to the menu
.RB ( n
or Esc).
.PP
The generated model is also written to
.B grmodels.csprite
in the current directory as the byte-identical CSprite stream the
original builds (SPT_MESH element: vertex and triangle counts,
CD3I32 vertices, CMeshTri triangles, SPT_END), in place of the
DolDoc cut-and-paste embedding, which has no counterpart here.
.PP
While a model is displayed, dragging with the left button rotates it
and the arrow keys yaw and pitch;
.B +
and
.B \-
zoom.
These viewing controls are a port addition; TempleOS shows the sprite
statically in the document.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B grmodels.csprite
the last generated model, raw CSprite bytes
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/grmodels.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The TempleOS fixed-point matrix arithmetic is emulated with rounded
real arithmetic, so vertex coordinates can differ from the original
by one unit.
Faces are depth-sorted rather than depth-buffered, so mutually
intersecting boxes can occasionally draw in the wrong order.
